    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily create-owner limit (reject the 101st owner of the day with **429**), following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `CheckOwnerDailyLimit.java` (function) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today; throws `DailyOwnerLimitException` when the count is \u2265 100. Mirrors the existing `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`/`CountOwnerNamesakes` style, including skipping the record being created.\n- `DailyOwnerLimitException.java` \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`).\n- `DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 429 (`HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`) with a `ProblemDetail`, matching the `CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler` pattern.\n- `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DailyOwnerLimitException.yml` \u2014 wires the handler.\n\n**Wiring:**\n- Inserted a `checkDailyLimit` step in `owners.POST.yml` between `checkCityCapacity` and `countNamesakes`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the count reflects only pre-existing owners.\n\nNew owners default to `registrationDate = today` in `BuildOwner`, so 100 creations today make the count reach 100 and the 101st is rejected \u2014 exactly what the `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` test asserts. Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS** (1 test, 0 failures).",
